{"title":"Career roadmap · Language Trainer","role":"Language Trainer","summary":"A Language Trainer teaches learners to develop practical proficiency in a foreign language through structured lessons, conversation practice, pronunciation, grammar, vocabulary, listening, reading and writing. A BA in a foreign language provides the core linguistic foundation, while proficiency certification, teaching methodology and practical training experience determine employability.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1","Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Foreign Languages (French, German, Spanish, Japanese, Korean, Chinese, Arabic)"},"about":[{"label":"Career-route check","text":"Strong direct alignment. The BA builds language proficiency, but professional teaching roles may require higher proficiency levels, recognised language certifications and/or a teaching qualification depending on the employer and country."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Typical route","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["BA Foreign Language","Language Teaching Internship/Assistantship","Language Trainer/Instructor","Senior Language Trainer","Academic Coordinator","Language Training Manager","Head of Language Training"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career objective"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Reach advanced proficiency, build teaching skills and obtain recognised language certification."}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Specialise in a language, learner segment or professional training domain and build classroom experience."}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Progress toward Senior Trainer, Academic Coordinator, Curriculum Designer or Language Programme Manager."}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Lead language-learning programmes, corporate training or establish an independent language-training business."}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["When","Build this","Learn from","Proof of progress","Gap it moves"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 1"},{"text":"Pronunciation, alphabet/script where applicable and basic grammar"},{"text":"University + native-language resources"},{"text":"A1-level assessment"},{"text":"Language foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 1 Sem 2"},{"text":"Everyday vocabulary and conversation"},{"text":"Language labs + speaking practice"},{"text":"A1/A2 assessment"},{"text":"Communication"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 1"},{"text":"Intermediate grammar and listening"},{"text":"Language courses + native media"},{"text":"A2/B1-level assessment"},{"text":"Fluency"}],[{"text":"Year 2 Sem 2"},{"text":"Teaching fundamentals"},{"text":"TESOL/teaching methodology resources"},{"text":"10 sample lesson plans"},{"text":"Pedagogy"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 1"},{"text":"Classroom practice"},{"text":"Language institute/internship"},{"text":"Teaching internship"},{"text":"Experience"}],[{"text":"Year 3 Sem 2"},{"text":"Advanced proficiency + curriculum design"},{"text":"Certification preparation"},{"text":"B2/C1 or equivalent where applicable"},{"text":"Professional readiness"}],[{"text":"Honours Year 4 Sem 1"},{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Research + teaching projects"},{"text":"Complete language course module"},{"text":"Expertise"}],[{"text":"Honours Year 4 Sem 2"},{"text":"Professional teaching portfolio"},{"text":"Live teaching + interviews"},{"text":"Demo class + CV + portfolio"},{"text":"Employability"}]]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"Target proficiency depends heavily on the language. For example, Japanese commonly uses JLPT levels, French uses CEFR/DELF-DALF, German uses CEFR/Goethe examinations, Spanish uses DELE/SIELE, and Korean uses TOPIK. Chinese and Arabic have their own recognised proficiency frameworks/examinations. Check the current official examination system for the chosen language."},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects to prioritise"},{"type":"list","items":[{"t